Baseline evaluation on the V11 tree. Gates first (written before any run), then results. Scripts stay on the maintainer's machine.

=== GATES ===
Marin baseline evaluation: workload limits and stopping gates (fixed before any measurement)

Tree: HEAD c36e076 plus the uncommitted V11 work; release binaries rebuilt from it. No source change in this milestone.
Tool: `marin-run bench` (+ --sample-gpu --json), run one cell at a time by benchmarks/evaluation/matrix.py. Nothing else uses the GPU.

Models used: every installed checkpoint with a supported path. Not measured: Granite-4.0-H-Tiny (no weights, header only),
Qwen3.5-4B BF16 on CUDA (does not fit 8 GB), Qwen3.5-4B BF16 on CPU (8.7 GB RSS against ~8 GB available), the *-Base twins of
Qwen3 (same architecture and code path as the measured chat models; used only for the HF checks that were made for them).

Cells:  prompt 128 / 512 / 1024 x 64 decode tokens, plus 128 x 32 decode tokens; fixed seed 0, temperature 0.
GPU:    warmup 1, runs 3.      CPU: warmup 1, runs 2 (models >= 2B: warmup 0, runs 1 at prompts 512 and 1024; labelled).
Long context (2k/4k/8k, 32 tokens, 1 run, warmup 0): Qwen3.5-4B Q8 CUDA, Qwen3.5-2B CUDA, Qwen3-1.7B CUDA (f16 KV); CPU: 0.6B to 2k.
Scalar fallback: MARIN_MATMUL_SCALAR=1, Qwen3-0.6B CPU, 128 x 32, 1 run.

Gates:
  G1 per cell timeout 600 s (long context 900 s); a timeout is recorded, never retried.
  G2 total GPU matrix stops at 90 min, CPU matrix at 120 min; unfinished cells are listed as not measured.
  G3 drift probe: Qwen3-0.6B CUDA 128x32 (3 runs) before, between and after the GPU matrix. Decode TPS spread over the probes
     <= 5% means the matrix is comparable inside itself; more means hardware drift and every cell is marked.
  G4 a cell starts only if the GPU is below 60 C and no marin, python or cargo process uses it (the desktop compositor and editor always hold ~240 MiB).
  G5 regression = same command, same session, paired against the accepted BENCHMARKS.md row, decode or prefill more than 10%
     slower after the drift probe is taken into account. A historical row alone is never proof.
  G6 numerical checks use the existing HF references only (tests/reference, bench-results); a reference made for a different
     model is not run. Granite thresholds are not changed: a known NO-GO miss is reported as a miss, not as a regression.
  G7 workflows: each feature runs only where it is supported; pass/fail is output correctness (greedy equal, state isolated,
     recovery) first, timing second. Source unchanged => the last full-suite result (816 + 816, HF PASS) stands; only focused checks rerun.

=== RESULTS ===
Marin baseline evaluation on the V11 tree (HEAD c36e076 + uncommitted V11 work; no source changed in this milestone)
RTX 5050 Laptop 8 GB at a 40 W cap, Ryzen 7 260 (16 threads), 14 GB RAM, Arch Linux, release binaries, fixed seed 0, temperature 0.
Gates and limits: plan.txt (written before the first run). Raw data: bench-results/evaluation/ (git-ignored; one JSON + text per cell).
Reproduce: python3 benchmarks/evaluation/matrix.py {probe,gpu,long,scalar,cpu}; paired.sh OLD_BIN OUT; verify.sh; parity.sh; coldload.sh;
           benchmarks/server_load.py; benchmarks/hibernation/measure.py; marin-run spec-bench (prompts: benchmarks/spec_prompts.sh).

