3. CLOCKS / POWER / HEAT (bench --sample-gpu)
   Cap 40 W. Big models run at the cap: 4B 36-39 W, 2B 33-39 W, 1.7B 30-37 W at 0.9-1.5 GHz; 0.6B 10-33 W at 1.4-1.8 GHz. Peak 62 C, no thermal slowdown.
   Probe (Qwen3-0.6B CUDA 128x32 decode): 148.0 (start, cool GPU) -> 185.3 -> 186.1. The later two agree within 0.4%; the first is 20% lower.
   => G3 fails for the first probe: the cells before probe 2 (the small Qwen3 models) are marked noisy. 0.6B/1.7B decode spread 20-90% between
      cells of one model comes from clock/launch variance, not software; do not read small-model cell-to-cell differences as findings.
   Large-model (4B, 2B, Granite-pair) cells repeat within 1-3%.
   GPU probe: memory 300 GB/s first, 262 GB/s sustained; fp32 11 TFLOP/s; bf16 tensor 27.8 TFLOP/s; power cap active in 67% of busy samples.

