     4B Q8 CPU      40.0 -> 41.1 (+2.8%)             4.50 -> 4.42 (-1.8%)
   V11 left the generation path unchanged. Against the BENCHMARKS.md rows the machine is slower today (4B CUDA decode 35.9 recorded vs
   32.1 now, -10%; 4B CPU 4.75 vs 4.3). A build of the older commit 8130ad7 measured now: 4B Q8 CUDA 512x32 decode 31.5/31.9 (new 32.4/32.1),
   prefill 131/127 (new 127/128). Same speed on old and new code => the gap to the recorded row is the machine (power cap, clocks, ambient),
   not software. CONFIRMED SOFTWARE REGRESSIONS: none.

5. NUMERICAL CHECKS (existing HF references only, marin-run verify)
   PASS: Qwen3-0.6B cpu+cuda, Qwen3-1.7B cpu+cuda, Qwen3-1.7B-Base cuda (max logit diff 1.5e-5 - 1.9e-5, token choices match);
         Qwen3.5-4B Q8 cuda (1.31e-5; normalized 3.879e-6, RMS 3.288e-6) and cpu; Qwen3.5-2B cuda, cpu, int8; Granite BF16 cpu.
   FAIL (known NO-GO, thresholds unchanged): Granite BF16 CUDA and Granite Q8 CPU pilot: case 2 (Python function) step 2, relative RMS 1.098e-5
         against the fixed 1e-5 gate (normalized 3.38e-6 passes); greedy tokens match. Same result as the archived decision: not a regression.
   Greedy parity (parity.sh): CPU vs CUDA equal for Qwen3-0.6B, 1.7B, Qwen3.5-2B-Base, 4B Q8, Granite; SIMD vs scalar equal.

6. END-TO-END WORKFLOWS (Qwen3.5-4B Q8 CUDA release unless stated)
   PASS  chat, fresh + 2 warm turns piped through `marin`: correct recall of name and number; save, new-process resume, correct answer.
   PASS  /checkpoint on a 1,121-token chat: state 127 MB saved in 1.0 s; resume with it 7 s total (1.02 s state load) vs 14 s re-reading the
         history; both answered correctly. Below 256 tokens the checkpoint is refused with a clear reason (by design).
   PASS  code mode (marin code .): 4 bounded read-only tool calls, correct answer, 24 s, context 1,513/8,192, log written.
   PASS  server concurrency (ctx 8192, up to 2 at once): 1 client 32-39 ev/s; 2 clients 49-50 ev/s aggregate (+40%, each 25-27/s);
         3rd client queues (TTFT 5.2 s) and is served; short requests next to a long prefill got first token in 0.16-0.67 s; no panics.
   PASS  speculation (opt-in, greedy, 128 tokens, 1 round): output identical to plain in all 8 prompts (same 2/2). Speed vs plain:
         edit-file 1.86x (58.6 vs 31.5 tok/s, 0.68 vs 1.27 J/tok), edit-diff 1.29x, chat 1.00x, fresh 1.00x (no loss).
   PASS  hibernation (3 cycles): process VRAM 4,696 -> 0 MiB, wake first token 4.2 s (load 3.9 s), warm 0.35 s, session reused 2,736-2,833, replayed 0.
         Power in this run: 20.0 W loaded-idle vs 14.6 W asleep (both P4); the earlier 90 s windows contradicted this (8.8 vs 9.1 W), so
         NO power saving is claimed: it depends on the P-state the card idles in.
   PASS  hot/cold sessions, 409/404, cancellation and hang-up, memory-pressure refusal and recovery, failed-wake stampede, repeated sleep/wake,
         changed-weights invalidation: cargo test server_cold (6), server_pressure (1), server_sleep (6) on the real 4B, 0 failed.
         Source unchanged since the last full-suite run (816 CUDA + 816 scalar passed, HF PASS), so the full suites were not rerun.
   Not run (unsupported by design): server/sessions/speculation on Qwen3, Granite, Qwen3.5-2B; Qwen3 GPU prefix snapshot (--snapshot) not exercised here.

7. BOTTLENECKS (profile: 4B Q8 CUDA 512x16)
   Prefill 4B CUDA (130 tok/s): MLP 50.6%, QKV 23.5%, attention-out 7.2% = 81% in the INT8 projections at 0.56-1.23 TFLOP/s (card: 11 fp32,
         27.8 bf16 tensor); DeltaNet recurrence 17.1%; attention 1.1%. Prefill falls from 130 to 94 tok/s at 8k as recurrence/attention grow.
   Decode 4B CUDA (31-33 tok/s, 142 GB/s effective of 262 sustained): MLP 37.6% at 206 GB/s, QKV 18.7% at only 92 GB/s, DeltaNet 12.8%,
         lm head 9.6% at 225 GB/s, norms 4.0%, state copy 2.5%, unaccounted 3.6%. Memory-bandwidth and power-cap limited, with QKV and DeltaNet below the bandwidth the MLP reaches.
   Decode, Qwen3 / Granite CUDA: 0.6B and Granite are launch- and clock-limited (6-7 ms/token at 224-366 GB/s); 1.7B/2B around 180 GB/s.
   CPU decode: effective weight read 19-22 GB/s with only 1.3-1.6 of 16 cores busy during decode (Granite INT8 reaches 65 GB/s); CPU prefill is
         multithreaded (8 threads) and compute-bound (40 - 640 tok/s by model).
   Loading: 2.5-4.6 s for 1-4 GB checkpoints, CPU/format-bound (cold cache adds <= 1.2 s). Sessions: restore 1 s per 1k tokens (checkpoint) or
         cold-host thaw; a 4B wake costs 3.9 s of load.
   Kind of each problem:  4B prefill = optimization opportunity.  4B decode = mostly hardware limit (power cap), partly QKV/DeltaNet kernels.
         4B / Granite CUDA gap to the recorded rows = hardware drift.  Granite CUDA RMS miss = known numerical NO-GO.  CPU decode single-core = opportunity.

8. TOP 3 OPTIMISATIONS (ranked; none started)
   1. Faster INT8 prefill for Qwen3.5 on CUDA (tensor-core or tiled dequantizing GEMM for MLP/QKV/out). Evidence: 81% of prefill at ~1 TFLOP/s on
      a card that sustains 11-27; 4B TTFT 7.7 s at 1k, 15.8 s at 2k, 87 s at 8k. Realistic 2-3x prefill (the card is power capped, so not the
      raw ratio). Benefit: every long prompt, code mode, restores, cold-session replays. Risk: numerics (HF gate 1e-4 / 1e-5), medium-high effort; no extra memory.
   2. Multithreaded CPU decode GEMV. Evidence: 1.3-1.6 cores busy and 19-22 GB/s at decode. Needs a CPU bandwidth probe first to know the ceiling
      (not measured); plausible 1.5-2.5x CPU decode on Qwen3/Qwen3.5 for the users without a GPU, which the spec targets. Risk: low (same math,
      scalar equal), small effort, no memory cost.
   3. Qwen3.5 decode kernels: QKV at 92 GB/s vs MLP 206 GB/s, DeltaNet 12.8%, norms/copies 6.5%. Closing QKV to MLP-level would save about 10% of
      decode time, i.e. ~3 tok/s; the rest is the power cap. Low user-visible gain, medium risk.
   Not recommended: more batching (2 clients already +40%); power savings from hibernation (unproven).

9. LIMITS OF THIS BASELINE
   One GPU, one session, 1-3 runs per cell (1 for 4B-CPU long prompts and the 2k-8k cells). Small CUDA models are noisy (point 3). Models were
   mostly warm in the page cache except in coldload. Qwen3-0.6B-Base, Qwen3 snapshot, Qwen3.5-2B CUDA INT8 were not measured. 8k+ Qwen3.5 contexts
   past 8192 and CPU contexts past 2k were not run (CPU 4B at 2k would take about 1 minute of prefill per request).
